{
 "id": "029-uyak-avi",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "The Rhyme Hunt",
 "theme": "Rhyming words (phonological awareness)",
 "blurb": "Caramel the cat and Wiggle the hedgehog want to write a song, but the words trip and stumble: click, clack. When Buzz the bee hums “Bee, tree! Cat, hat!”, a rhyme hunt begins in the meadow!",
 "voiceNames": {
  "karamel": "Caramel (cat)",
  "kipir": "Wiggle (hedgehog)",
  "vizviz": "Buzz (bee)"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "One sunny autumn morning, Caramel the cat and Wiggle the hedgehog had a picnic in the meadow. Caramel stroked her whiskers: “Let's write a song!” Wiggle's spikes wiggled with joy.",
   "hits": {
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Let's write a song!"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "A song? Hooray!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Caramel!",
   "ask": "Have you ever made up a song? If you wrote a song with a friend, what would it be about?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Caramel began: “In the sky, a cloud so white…” Wiggle added: “…on the ground, a ball!” Click, clack, plop! The song stumbled. Caramel was cross; her tail puffed up. Wiggle felt sad and curled up like a ball.",
   "hits": {
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Oh no! The song's not working!"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "Our words didn't fit together…"
    },
    "bulut": {
     "say": "In the sky, a cloud so white…"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Wiggle!",
   "ask": "Why did Caramel's tail puff up? When something doesn't go the way you want, how do you feel, and what do you do?",
   "cues": [
    {
     "w": 16,
     "fx": "click"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Caramel took a deep breath and smiled at Wiggle. Just then, Buzz the bee flew by. “Bee, tree! Cat, hat!” she hummed. Wiggle was amazed: “The endings sound the same!” Buzz laughed: “That's called a rhyme!” Caramel giggled: “A hat? I'm not wearing a hat!”",
   "hits": {
    "vizviz": {
     "say": "Bzzz! Bee, tree! Cat, hat!"
    },
    "karamel": {
     "say": "A hat? I'm not wearing a hat!"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "The endings match! Hedgehog, wedgehog!"
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "How do you think the song will go this time?",
    "res": "Let's see!",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "They find matching words"
     },
     {
      "l": "They ask Buzz"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Buzz!",
   "ask": "How do “bee” and “tree” end? Can you make up a funny word that rhymes with your name?"
  },
  {
   "text": "The rhyme hunt began! What came out of the basket? Melon, orange, banana and honey! Buzz whispered: “Listen to the endings!” Caramel pricked up her ears: “Melon to munch… munch… Where's its rhyme?” Wiggle rolled the orange: “Orange so sunny… sunny… Which one rhymes?” You find the pairs too!",
   "hits": {
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Melon to munch… munch… Where's its rhyme?"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "Orange so sunny… sunny… Which one rhymes?"
    },
    "karpuz": {
     "say": "Melon to munch, banana for lunch!"
    },
    "muz": {
     "say": "Melon to munch, banana for lunch!"
    },
    "portakal": {
     "say": "Orange so sunny, golden honey!"
    },
    "bal": {
     "say": "Orange so sunny, golden honey!"
    },
    "vizviz": {
     "say": "Bzzz! Listen to the ending!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Melon to munch, banana for lunch! Orange so sunny, golden honey!",
    "msg": "You found the rhymes!"
   },
   "hint": "Find the pairs!",
   "ask": "How do “munch” and “lunch” end? What else could go in the basket to make a rhyme?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Caramel sang again: “In the sky, a cloud so white…” Wiggle listened to the ending and added: “…on the ground, an acorn sleeps tight!” The song rolled along, clickety-clack! Buzz buzzed: “There are more pairs in the meadow. Which one goes with which?” You find them too!",
   "hits": {
    "karamel": {
     "say": "In the sky, a cloud so white…"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "…on the ground, an acorn sleeps tight!"
    },
    "bulut": {
     "say": "Cloud so white, acorn sleeps tight!"
    },
    "palamut": {
     "say": "Cloud so white, acorn sleeps tight!"
    },
    "cicek": {
     "say": "Flower so red, ladybird on its head!"
    },
    "bocek": {
     "say": "Flower so red, ladybird on its head!"
    },
    "vizviz": {
     "say": "Bzzz! There are more pairs!"
    },
    "limon": {
     "say": "Lemon so round, balloon off the ground!"
    },
    "balon": {
     "say": "Lemon so round, balloon off the ground!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Cloud so white, acorn sleeps tight! Flower so red, ladybird on its head! Lemon so round, balloon off the ground!",
    "msg": "You matched them all!"
   },
   "hint": "Find the pairs!",
   "ask": "Why didn't the song stumble this time? Can you find another word that rhymes with “ground”?"
  },
  {
   "text": "At sunset, the three friends sang their song: “A cloud so white, an acorn sleeps tight! A flower so red, a ladybird on its head! Caramel, Buzz and Wiggle, we wrote this song, now giggle!” The words held hands, just like friends.",
   "hits": {
    "karamel": {
     "say": "Writing a song with you is wonderful!"
    },
    "kipir": {
     "say": "A flower so red, a ladybird on its head!"
    },
    "vizviz": {
     "say": "Bzzz! Again, again!"
    },
    "bulut": {
     "say": "A cloud so white in the sky!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Sing the song together!",
   "ask": "Let's sing the song together! What rhyming song would you write with a friend?"
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "Notices rhyming words and compares the final sounds of words (TAEOB.3, unverified)",
   "Chooses to listen to chants and songs, and listens to them (TADB.1)",
   "Retells the events of a story in the order they happened (TADB.3)",
   "Creates a shared product (a song) together with a friend (SDB2.2 Cooperation)"
  ],
  "once": [
   "Show the cover and ask: What might the cat, the hedgehog and the bee be doing?",
   "Game: I'll say my name, and we find a word that ends the same way (Emma–bemma).",
   "Rhyming words are words that sound the same at the end, like “cat” and “hat”."
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "On page 2, ask why the song stumbled.",
   "On the matching pages (4 and 5), say each picture's little chant together before the child touches it; the spoken reply only comes after the right pair."
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "Sing the song together while clapping.",
   "Put the events in order: the song didn't work → Buzz arrived → the rhyme hunt → the song.",
   "Play with made-up rhymes (E2.5 Playfulness)."
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "The Rhyme Basket",
   "sure": "15 min",
   "materyal": "A basket; wordless picture cards in rhyming pairs (cat–hat, bee–tree, moon–spoon, frog–log) and 2 odd-one-out cards (e.g. apple, ball)",
   "adim": [
    "Take the cards out of the basket one by one and say their names.",
    "The children find the pair that ends the same way and put the card next to it.",
    "Make up a two-line song as a class with the pairs you found."
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "Why didn't the song work the first time?",
   "Is there a funny word that rhymes with your name?",
   "How did you feel when you made something together with a friend?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Rhyme hunt in the kitchen",
   "d": "Find rhyming pairs in the kitchen together: spoon–moon, dish–fish, cup–up, pan–man. Made-up words are allowed too!"
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read “The Rhyme Hunt”. Caramel and Wiggle wrote a song together by finding words that end with the same sound (munch–lunch, red–head). At home you can go on a rhyme hunt as a game. Nonsense words that rhyme also support sound awareness at this age."
 },
